<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lingaraja Temple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lingaraja Temple is the largest temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhubaneswar">Bhubaneswar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harihara">Harihara</a>. Built in the 11th century, mainly under the Somavamshi kings, it is the high point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga">Kalinga</a> style, with a curving tower about 55 m high rising over a walled compound of many smaller shrines. It remains an active place of worship, closed to non-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lingaraja-temple.jpg" alt="Lingaraja Temple" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Satyakam Parthasarathy · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lingaraj_Temple_,_Bhubaneswar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
